I'm not entirely sure you did it right, because the patch bit you quoted
looked a little bit odd to me; a lot of + and not much corresponding -,
so I couldn't determine the precise history of what you changed.

What you're looking for are any cases where the code asks:

if (uarm->otyp == GDSM || uarm->otyp == GDS)

...without confirming that the player's actually wearing armor first
(by checking to see if uarm is defined -- either on that line, or
earlier in the function).  The line below is an effective way to fix the 
problem, ie. turning the above fragment into:

if (uarm && (uarm->otyp == GDSM || uarm->otyp == GDS))

...which will short-circuit prior to checking uarm->otyp if uarm isn't
defined, thus preventing a segfault.

